From: vigaz <pudimdebacon3@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 21 Sep 2026 14:25:45 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 7/7] kernel manager: wire GPU sliders to the real
 LIMIT_AXION_USER range limiter

Replaces the single-value OPP lock (fix_target_opp_index) with a genuine
min/max range: addGpuRangeIfPresent() detects the new axion_gpu_range
kernel node and takes priority over both the old lock and the decorative
devfreq min_freq/max_freq pair. Since axion_gpu_range takes one combined
write ("ceiling floor"), not one value per path, writeGpuRange() looks
up the sibling control (min when writing max, or vice versa), reads its
last persisted value, and writes both together.

Change-Id: I0adbe1433872dd2d54d84e3d689c884e09f75655
---
